1
00:00:00,533 --> 00:00:03,500
Water can get hotter than boiling — and still not boil.

2
00:00:03,933 --> 00:00:05,866
Boiling needs somewhere to start.

3
00:00:05,966 --> 00:00:09,367
Bubbles usually form around tiny impurities in the water.

4
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:16,200
Heat plain water by itself in a very clean cup, and it can climb past boiling while looking completely calm.

5
00:00:16,667 --> 00:00:22,972
Then a small disturbance — picking up the cup, adding a spoonful of coffee — and bubbles burst out all at once.

6
00:00:23,072 --> 00:00:25,367
Boiling water can erupt from the cup.

7
00:00:25,867 --> 00:00:29,463
So don't heat water longer than the instructions recommend.

8
00:00:29,563 --> 00:00:34,300
And adding instant coffee or sugar before heating greatly reduces the risk.

9
00:00:34,733 --> 00:00:36,963
Calm doesn't always mean below boiling.

10
00:00:37,063 --> 00:00:40,200
That water may just be waiting for a reason to boil.
